<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tadla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1554</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tadla was fought in September 1554 near Tadla in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> between the Saadi sultan Muhammad al-Shaykh and the Wattasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-abu-hassun">Ali Abu Hassun</a>, who had retaken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> earlier that year with Ottoman troops from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. Abu Hassun was defeated and killed, ending the Wattasid dynasty and leaving the Saadis masters of Morocco.</p></div>
